  "verbalization": "Khrinone C is shown to have a target relationship with CCF-STTG1 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link being its interaction with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase. This enzyme is also a target of 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, which further reinforces the connection to CCF-STTG1. The indirect pathway through Ataxin-2, which is targeted by Khrinone C, appears to be a secondary route that may contribute to the overall relationship. The evidence suggests that Khrinone C may act through a metabolic or enzymatic pathway involving sialyltransferases, ultimately influencing CCF-STTG1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Khrinone C in modulating the activity of CCF-STTG1 via a complex network of targets, emphasizing the importance of sialyltransferases in the drug's mechanism of action.",
